     "construction": {
      "name": "complete_native_box_product",
      "proof": "Complete-owner cubical product and common restoration\n\nLet a complete native packing of m copies of a canonical solid P lie in\na cube of side t centered at c0. Subtract c0 from every source center.\nFor q in {2,3}, put b_z=t*(z-(q-1)/2*(1,1,1)) for every ordered grid word\nz in {0,...,q-1}^3. The q^3 boxes b_z+[-t/2,t/2]^3 have disjoint interiors\nand fill [-qt/2,qt/2]^3. Copy every complete source owner into each box,\nkeeping its actual quaternion. This gives q^3*m jointly compatible whole\nowners. Within a box, compatibility is the source packing. Between boxes,\none actual coordinate wall separates their complete containing boxes.\nNo pair is allowed to choose an independent box location or host scale.\n\nFor native restoration let rho=10000001/10000000. Apply rho to EVERY\nconstructed center while retaining the unit solid and quaternion. Because\nthe origin is interior to every canonical body, each support value is\npositive: a separator gap gains (rho-1) times its two support values,\nand a host-wall margin gains (rho-1) times the owner's support value.\nThus the entire packing remains strictly disjoint inside side rho*q*t.\nThe final host side is rounded outward with an additional 1e-7. Each\ncenter is evaluated as an exact rational then rounded once to binary64;\nthe final native certificate verifies that rounding on every pair/wall.\n\nThe complete grid-word/source-owner decoder is retained. A smaller count\nis its literal ordered whole-owner prefix; no remaining center or frame\nchanges. Classical Cartesian products and every donor's original author\nand method remain attributed. No global optimum or original discovery of\nthe Cartesian-product operation is asserted.\n",
